  "source_findings": [
    "Supported geometry is getpagesize()==4096; checked anonymous private read/write mmap supplies8192 bytes. Every original byte is initialized with deterministic bounded-offset volatile writes.",
    "One mprotect(base+1,4096,PROT_NONE) must return -1 with errno EINVAL22. Every original8192 byte is then volatile-read and compared; this checks accessibility and preservation beyond errno alone.",
    "Writes/readback at offsets0,4096,8191 check both pages and final byte after refusal. This checks three boundary writes, not exhaustive post-refusal writes across all bytes.",
    "One successful munmap is required before exact73B success stdout; no pointer use follows unmap. Failure exits nonzero with diagnostic stderr; process-owned mappings on failure are not falsely reported as released.",
    "No fault handler, fork, pointer guessing, kernel mutation or default capability activation is introduced."
  ],
